Z||000000||DrRodey||12-15-2000||03:22 PM||||Ok here's the situation.  Couple months ago my batt. wasn't holding dick for a charge so i took it and the alt out cause it was still stock.  Had both tested, both needed to be replaced so i did.  Since then the belt as sounded like a druged up chipmunk it squeeked so dang much.  Today went and started it up again to keep fluids moving ect.  no squeek... cool one problem fixed right?/? WRONG  Now my volt guage is redlineing on me.. what went wrong?<P>------------------<BR>'88 Formula CONVERTABLE<BR>'85 Coupe<BR>     <IMG SRC="http://freepages.ugo.com/RodeysPlace/files/fieroPage.JPG">     <BR> <A HREF="http://freepages.ugo.com/RodeysPlace/HomePlace.html" TARGET=_blank>freepages.ugo.com/RodeysPlace/HomePlace.html</A>||||reg||8
Z||000001||rogergarrison||12-15-2000||07:02 PM||||Did needle stay on high charge, or go down after it ran awile? If it stays up, sounds like maybe a short, even internally in alt. theres a built it regulator inside, youll have to replace it (hope u have your warranty papers)||||reg||1
Z||000002||Raydar||12-15-2000||08:07 PM||||DrRodey,<P>Are you sure the belt is tight? Mine sat for a few days without being driven. Started it up last night, after several days of being rained on. Volt gauge showed about 1/4 scale.<BR>Let the engine run for a few seconds, heard the belt squeal for a second as it caught traction, then volt gauge jumped to 1/2..3/4 scale. Does this pretty much whenever it gets rained on.||||reg||1
Z||000003||DrRodey||12-15-2000||08:35 PM||||I had it running for about 10 minnutes and it stayed up the entire time.  Also It does sit most of the time now that it is winter, inside a heated garage.  I start it once or twice a week and drive it around the garage to keep fluids moving and keep it loose.  I think the belt is tight .. tightned it as much as the two of us could when we put the new alt in.||||reg||1
Z||000004||theogre||12-15-2000||11:07 PM||||You need to get it to a shop. many of the chain shops and K/Wal-mart with autocenter will do this test free.<P>disconnect the battery between runs if it is going to sit more than a week or so. That should help some. Consider one of the switches you can add for this purpose to make life easier. JC Whitless and most performance shops have them. chains like pep boys or autozone might. RVs and boats use them allot.||||reg||1
